$2x + 7y = -37$

What is the value of $x + y$ for the solution $(x, y)$ to the system of equations above?', NULL, $lyceon_json$[{"key":"A","text":"$-1$"},{"key":"B","text":"$6$"},{"key":"C","text":"$-6$"},{"key":"D","text":"$-4$"}]$lyceon_json$::jsonb, 'C', NULL, E'Multiplying the second equation by 2 gives $4x + 14y = -74$. Subtracting the first equation from this result yields $17y = -85$, so $y = -5$. Substituting back into $4x - 3(-5) = 11$ gives $4x + 15 = 11$, so $4x = -4$ and $x = -1$. Therefore $x + y = -1 + (-5) = -6$. The distractor $-1$ is only the value of $x$, not the requested sum. The distractor 6 comes from a sign error that negates the correct answer. The distractor $-4$ results from an arithmetic slip in combining the values.', $lyceon_json${"A":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"partial_reasoning"},"B":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"sign_error"},"C":{"role":"correct","error_taxonomy":null},"D":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"arithmetic_slip"}}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, NULL, 'draft', 1, 75, false, $lyceon_json${"provenance":"Lyceon original","authored_by":"claude","authored_date":"2026-08-27"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, $lyceon_json${"model":"claude","generation_date":"2026-08-27","prompt_version":"questions_governance_v1"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb);




























