For what value of $k$ does the system of equations above have no solution?', NULL, $lyceon_json$[]$lyceon_json$::jsonb, '-8', ARRAY['-8'], E'A system of two linear equations has no solution when the lines are parallel but not identical. This occurs when the ratios of the coefficients of $x$ and $y$ are equal but the ratio of the constants is different. Setting $\\frac{6}{k} = \\frac{-9}{12}$ gives $\\frac{6}{k} = -\\frac{3}{4}$, so $k = -8$. Checking the constant ratio: $\\frac{14}{-7} = -2$, which is not equal to $-\\frac{3}{4}$, confirming the system is inconsistent (parallel, non-coincident lines) when $k = -8$.', NULL, NULL, 'draft', 1, 100, false, $lyceon_json${"provenance":"Lyceon original","authored_by":"claude","authored_date":"2026-08-27"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, $lyceon_json${"model":"claude","generation_date":"2026-08-27","prompt_version":"questions_governance_v1"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb);




